WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.130
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here.

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:07.390
As you might have been hoping, Captain America
Civil War has 2 post-credit scenes.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:11.300
One which appears just after the credits for
the main cast and crew, and another after

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.300
the full set of credits has finished rolling.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:18.060
In this video I’m going to talk about both
these scenes and just to be clear there are

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.060
spoilers ahead, so you want to avoid those
you can watch my spoiler-free review right

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.060
here.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:26.800
The mid-credits start with Bucky being tended
to by a doctor in a super high-tech medical

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.840
facility and his metal arm is still missing
from when it was blasted off by Iron Man in

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.840
the movie.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.449
We then see Steve Rogers there with Bucky
and he asks his friend, "You sure about this?"

00:00:35.449 --> 00:00:40.149
to which Bucky replies "I can't trust my own
mind so until they figure out how to get this

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:44.269
stuff outta my head, I think going back under
is the best thing for everybody."

00:00:44.269 --> 00:00:49.609
Bucky is then strapped into an upright cryo-chamber
and frozen, a nod to the flashback scene in

00:00:49.609 --> 00:00:54.050
The Winter Soldier film where Zola orders
Bucky to be put on ice and also a call back

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:58.399
to how he was put into cryostasis by the Russians
in the Captain America comics while they figured

00:00:58.399 --> 00:00:59.620
out what to do with him.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.549
The camera then cuts to Black Panther and
Captain America.

00:01:02.549 --> 00:01:07.080
Steve Rogers thanks T'Challa who responds
"Your friend and my father, they were both

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.080
victims.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:09.640
If I can help one of them find peace."

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.010
The advanced medical centre reflects the fact
that in the Marvel comics, Wakanda is a wealthy

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.680
and technologically advanced nation thanks
to its vibranium deposits.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.409
It looks like the Wakandan doctors and scientists
might work on how to erase the HYDRA programming

00:01:22.409 --> 00:01:23.649
from Bucky's brain.

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:27.799
Rogers then warns that "if they find out he's
here, they'll come for him" to which Black

00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:30.119
Panther responds "let them try".

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.090
The camera then pans away from the medical
centre to a view of a misty jungle location

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:37.390
with a waterfall and mountains in the background
and a huge black panther statue.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:43.359
So this is a pretty cool tease for the 2018
Black Panther movie with an intriguing peek

00:01:43.359 --> 00:01:46.579
at what Wakanda looks like in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe.

00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:50.460
And with Marvel Studios president and producer
Kevin Feige saying that the Black Panther

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:55.040
movie has important links to Infinity War
Part 1, it looks likely we'll see Bucky brought

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.539
back for both those movies, and possibly we'll
also see some Avengers, or someone else coming

00:01:59.539 --> 00:02:01.549
after Bucky in the Black Panther movie.

00:02:01.549 --> 00:02:05.759
By the way, there's a really cool easter egg
to do with Bucky being shut down in the mid-credits

00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:06.759
scene.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:11.490
The working title of Civil War was "Sputnik",
and in the comics "Sputnik" is the safeword

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:15.910
that the Russians implanted in Bucky as a
safety mechanism to shut him down in case

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:19.820
he went crazy, a bit like how the other Winter
Soldiers in this movie turn against their

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:20.820
guards.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:24.740
Moving on to the post-credits, this scene
starts with Peter Parker in his bedroom with

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:28.110
Aunt May calling and asking him who it was
who hit him.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:32.170
Peter replies "some guy" while he's fiddling
with what looks like his web shooter around

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.170
his wrist.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:37.220
It's a call back to the airport fight scene
and when Aunt May asks what the guy's name

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:41.260
is, Peter replies "Steve", in other words
Steve Rogers.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:45.810
Aunt May asks if it's Steve from 12-C, the
guy with overbite, but Peter says that "he's

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.430
from Brooklyn" which is where Captain America
is from.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.840
The mention of 12-C could be a little easter
egg to the price of the first Spider-Man comic

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:53.840
which cost 12 cents.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.950
And the point about 'the overbite' is a funny
call-back to Tony Stark telling Cap in this

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:00.760
movie that "Sometimes I want to punch you
in your perfect teeth."

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:04.900
As Peter's talking to Aunt May, he activates
the shooter which sends a beam of light up

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:09.040
onto the ceiling, but he hides it away quickly
when Aunt May comes in the room.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.180
May asks him more about the fight and Peter
mentions that Steve's friend is huge, a funny

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:15.980
reference to his fight with Giant-Man at the
airport.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:20.700
Aunt May then leaves, and Peter uncovers his
arm with the camera panning up to reveal a

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.920
beam projecting a very cool Spidey symbol
on to the ceiling.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.700
The film then ends with the words "Spider-Man
will return."

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:31.420
So this piece of tech is likely something
Tony Stark has made or enhanced for Peter

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:35.870
Parker, remember we already saw Tony create
an Iron Man glove out of a hi-tech device

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:37.560
on his wrist in this movie.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:41.920
And Peter Parker's device is very much like
the Spider signal that Spider-Man has attached

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:42.970
to his belt in the comics.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:48.090
By the way, given that Tony Stark's former
science bro Bruce Banner, aka the Hulk, is

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:52.620
currently AWOL, I really like the way Tony
and Peter seem to be on their way to becoming

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:57.200
the new science bros, with Tony likely having
provided Peter with his new Spidey suit for

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.500
the airport fight.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:02.680
And with Robert Downey Jr now confirmed to
appear in Spider-Man Homecoming, it's a cool

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:07.130
hint that we can expect more tech geeking
out with Iron Man and Spider-Man in the 2017

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:08.130
solo movie.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:12.480
OK guys, that's the mid-credits and post-credits
scenes from Captain America Civil War.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.410
If you've seen the movie already, do you have
any cool theories about what they might mean

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:17.620
for future MCU movies?

